meta {
  name: Services
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_services
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("has the three lists and no backup[]", function () {
    const m = res.body.message;
    expect(m.implementation).to.be.an("array");
    expect(m.amc).to.be.an("array");
    expect(m.hosting).to.be.an("array");
    expect(m).to.not.have.property("backup");
  });

  test("project status and health are lowercase codes", function () {
    const m = res.body.message;
    const isCode = (v) => v === null || /^[a-z0-9_]+$/.test(v);
    m.implementation.concat(m.amc).forEach(function (p) {
      expect(p.status).to.satisfy(isCode);
      if (p.kind === "implementation") {
        expect(p.health).to.satisfy(isCode);
      }
    });
    m.amc.forEach(function (p) {
      expect(p).to.have.property("hours_included");
      expect(p).to.not.have.property("next_milestone");
    });
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Lists the client's services. No billing data. Home and the Services tab both read this one call.

  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_services`  
  **Screens:** Home (service cards), Services tab

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.

  **Query parameters:**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response:** three lists.

  - `implementation[]`: implementation projects. Same fields as `get_projects` with `kind: implementation`.
  - `amc[]`: AMC projects. Same fields as `get_projects` with `kind: amc`.
  - `hosting[]`: servers. Same fields as `get_servers`.

  `backup[]` was removed. Backup status is now on each `hosting[]` item (`last_backup`, `overdue`).

  ```json
  {
    "message": {
      "implementation": [
        {
          "name": "PROJ-0029",
          "title": "ERPNext Implementation - Hamza Trading",
          "display_title": "ERPNext Implementation",
          "kind": "implementation",
          "status": "active",
          "start_date": "2026-08-01",
          "end_date": "2026-12-31",
          "days_left": 55,
          "project_manager": "Sahana",
          "stage": "Data Migration",
          "phase": { "index": 3, "count": 8, "name": "Data Migration" },
          "health": "green",
          "percent": 40,
          "go_live_date": "2026-12-15",
          "go_live_days_left": 39,
          "next_milestone": { "title": "Configuration complete", "end_date": "2026-11-20", "days_left": 14, "status": "in_progress" }
        }
      ],
      "amc": [
        {
          "name": "PROJ-0030",
          "title": "AMC - Hamza Trading",
          "display_title": "AMC",
          "kind": "amc",
          "status": "amc",
          "start_date": "2026-01-01",
          "end_date": "2026-12-31",
          "days_left": 55,
          "project_manager": "Sahana",
          "contract_status": "active",
          "elapsed_percent": 85,
          "hours_used": 12.5,
          "hours_included": 40,
          "tickets": { "open": 2, "closed": 9 }
        }
      ],
      "hosting": [
        {
          "name": "SRV-0001",
          "server_name": "hamza-erp-prod",
          "site_url": "erp.hamza.sa",
          "environment": "Production",
          "provider": "OCI",
          "region": "me-jeddah-1",
          "region_label": "Jeddah",
          "status": "online",
          "status_checked_at": "2026-11-06T09:30:00+03:00",
          "erpnext_version": "v15.40.0",
          "backup_schedule": "Daily 02:00 AST, 14-day retention",
          "backup_frequency": "Daily, 02:00 AST",
          "backup_retention": "14 days + weekly offsite",
          "backup_policy_name": "OCI Gold",
          "last_backup": { "at": "2026-11-06T02:00:12+03:00", "state": "confirmed" },
          "overdue": false,
          "ssl_expiry": "2027-02-10",
          "ssl_days_left": 96,
          "last_restore_test": "2026-10-15"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```

  **Field notes:**

  - `display_title`: `title` without the customer name. Show this one.
  - `status` (projects): lowercase code of the project's implementation status: `discovery`, `active`, `go_live`, `hypercare`, `closed` (implementation) or `amc` (AMC). Null when not set.
  - `end_date`: the project's expected end date, else its deadline. `days_left` is counted from it (negative when past, null when no date).
  - `stage`: raw label (e.g. `"Data Migration"`), not a code. `phase.name` is the same label.
  - `phase`: null when the project's stage isn't one of the known phases.
  - `health`: `green`, `amber`, `red`, or null.
  - `go_live_date`: the go-live date, else the project deadline. Null when neither is set.
  - `next_milestone`: first milestone (in table order, of the project's contract type) not yet completed, or completed and waiting for sign-off. Null when none. Its `status` is a code: `not_started`, `in_progress`, `partially_completed`, `on_hold`, `due` or `completed`; its `days_left` is null once completed.
  - `contract_status` (AMC only): `active`, `expiring` (30 days or less left) or `expired`. Null when the project has no end date.
  - `elapsed_percent` (AMC only): 0-100 share of the contract period gone. Null when start or end date is missing.
  - `hours_used` (AMC only): sum of actual hours on the project's tasks. `hours_included` (AMC only): hours in the contract, null when not set (or 0).
  - AMC items have no `stage`, `phase`, `health`, `percent`, `go_live_date`, `go_live_days_left` or `next_milestone`.
  - `status` (hosting): `online`, `degraded`, `offline`, or null if never checked.
  - `environment` (hosting): raw label (`Production`, `Staging`, `Dev`). `region_label` is null for regions it doesn't know.
  - `backup_frequency`, `backup_retention` (hosting): short text written by our team, e.g. `"Daily, 02:00 AST"` and `"14 days + weekly offsite"`. Null until filled in. `backup_schedule` is still sent (free text).
  - `backup_policy_name`: null when there's no OCI data for the server.
  - `last_backup.state`: `confirmed`, `running`, `queued`, `failed`, `deleted`, or `recorded` (entered by hand, not read from OCI). Any other OCI state is passed through in lowercase, so treat unknown values as "unknown". `last_backup` is null when there's no data.
  - `overdue`: true when there's no confirmed backup in the last 26 hours **and** the server has a backup policy (OCI) or a `backup_schedule` (recorded backups). It is `false`, not null, for a server with no policy or schedule. Null only when there's no OCI data and no recorded backup at all.
  - Date fields are `YYYY-MM-DD`. Datetime fields are ISO 8601 with an offset.

  **Method:** GET. The server does not refuse a POST, but use GET.

  **Errors:**

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403** `no_client_linked`: the user isn't linked to any client company.
  - **403** `not_permitted`: `customer` was sent and isn't the user's company.
}
